# Shell scripts are the repository's executable surface and its lint surface
# (bin/*.sh, bin/backends/*.sh, tests/*.sh - the canonical set bin/fm-lint.sh
# owns). Checking them out with CRLF on Windows breaks both: POSIX shells read
# the carriage return as part of every token, and ShellCheck reports SC1017
# "Literal carriage return" on every line, so the lint gate fails on the file
# endings instead of on the code. Pin them to LF so a Windows checkout under
# core.autocrlf=true still produces the exact bytes CI lints.
*.sh text eol=lf
